/P 145 0 R
/E (The global economy demonstrates remarkable resilience entering 2026. According to the IMF's January 2026 World Economic Outlook Update, global growth is projected at 3.3% for 2026, revised slightly upward from October 2025 estimates. This growth is underpinned by technology investment, fiscal and monetary support, and private sector adaptability offsetting trade policy shifts. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
185 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 145 0 R
/E (Regional divergence remains a defining characteristic. The United States continues to exhibit economic exceptionalism, with forecasts ranging from 2.0% to 2.6% growth. Strong household finances, AI-driven investment, and supportive fiscal policy through tax cuts are key drivers. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
