/S /P
/P 145 0 R
/E (Global headline inflation is projected to decline to 3.1% in 2026 from 3.4% in 2025. However, the path remains uneven: U.S. inflation will return to target more gradually due to tariff impacts and immigration restrictions, while the eurozone may undershoot the ECB's 2% target. Goldman Sachs Research expects developed-market policy rates to converge lower, with the U.S. Federal Reserve projected to reduce rates by 50 basis points to 3.0-3.25%.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [6]
>>
